##  Bonus: Customizing a Live Nginx Website
On a separate EC2 instance running Nginx, I edited `/usr/share/nginx/html/index.html`:

1. Took a backup first: `sudo cp index.html index.html.bak`
2. Added a full-screen anime background using CSS `background: url(...) no-repeat center / cover`
3. Applied a Google Font (`Creepster`) for the title
4. Moved the heading below the image's focal point with Flexbox (`align-items: flex-end`)
5. Added a CSS `@keyframes` **blood-drip animation** under the text
6. Verified with `sudo systemctl status nginx` and a hard refresh in the browser

